{"step_index":1148,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T19:16:38Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Initialization**\n\nI've just observed the initialization sequence. It appears the window manager and hotkey manager are both up and running, and the system hotkeys have been successfully registered. The hook has been added, and the webview component is ready to go. Looks like a solid start!\n\n\n**Observing Navigation Completion**\n\nI've noted the successful return of `EnsureCoreWebView2Async` and the resolution of the web folder. The virtual host mapping and script addition are complete, with navigation to the specified URL now underway. Further, I see `MainWindow_Loaded` has completed. Now, I see the navigation completed, but I'm checking the result. A delay is applied, and then the window manager attempts to apply capture protection.\n\n\n**Investigating Crash Cause**\n\nI've pinpointed the crash! It occurred precisely when `ApplyCaptureProtection` ran, after navigation. It seems `SetWindowDisplayAffinity` with `WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE` is the culprit. The process died without logging the \"Applied\" message. Diving into the code, I see that the function is being called, but the documentation shows this specific call is problematic when the window has layered styles or lacks certain attributes, which I will now investigate.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\Arthur Henrique\\\\Documents\\\\GitHub\\\\Spectra\\\\src-csharp\\\\Platform\\\\WindowManager.cs\"","EndLine":"45","StartLine":"20","toolAction":"\"Viewing ApplyCaptureProtection in WindowManager.cs\"","toolSummary":"\"View ApplyCaptureProtection\""}}]}
